{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.PiBlockSeparation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.PiBlockSeparation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Subalgebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Pi","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.eq_top_of_separating_of_blockSurj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.eq_top_of_separating_of_blockSurj","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/PiBlockSeparation.lean#L136-L143","doc":"**The packaged criterion.**  A subalgebra whose scalar tuples separate the blocks and whose\nblock projections are surjective is the whole product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.eq_top_of_piSingle_of_blockSurj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.eq_top_of_piSingle_of_blockSurj","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/PiBlockSeparation.lean#L115-L134","doc":"**Block idempotents plus per-block surjectivity give everything.**  Any target is the sum of\nits blocks, and each block is `(Pi.single i 1) · aᵢ` for a preimage `aᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.piSingle_one_mem_of_separating","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.piSingle_one_mem_of_separating","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/PiBlockSeparation.lean#L52-L113","doc":"**Separating scalar tuples put every block idempotent in the subalgebra.**  Finite Lagrange\ninterpolation: for each `j ≠ i` pick a tuple separating `i` from `j`, and multiply the normalised\ndifferences.  The product is `1` in block `i` and `0` in every other block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.piScalarHom_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.piScalarHom_apply","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/PiBlockSeparation.lean#L49-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.piScalarHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.piScalarHom","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/PiBlockSeparation.lean#L43-L46","doc":"The scalar-tuple ring hom `(ι → R) →+* (∀ i, B i)`, `p ↦ fun i => algebraMap R (B i) (p i)`.\nThis is what lets the interpolation product be taken in a commutative ring. ","signatureChunk":0}]}